> It keeps crashing because it's too much data when dask goes to compute things. I think part of the problem is that we're combining all the regions, when actually we can put each station into 1 region, based on that region's bounding box. Can you make the following edits:
> 1. Don't combine up the regions into one dataset.
> 2. When going through the data, first split on the station ID. All entries with the same station ID will have the same lat,lon.
> 3. Find which region this lat,lon is contained in, using the latitude, longitude values to get its bounding box (plus 0.05 degrees on any side, since the grid resolution is 0.1).
> 4.. Just do the extraction using the data from the region that each station is within.
